{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower","id":940787,"title":"Still no errata for Praxis spam for recharging Mana and Willpower?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T13:11:57-07:00","id":940787,"title":"Still no errata for Praxis spam for recharging Mana and Willpower?","content":"According to DaveB, if you are casting magic under time constraints and/or pressure and fail, you take a cumulative -1 penalty on subsequent attempts. If you are under neither time constraints nor pressure, you must use the &quot;down and dirty spellcasting&quot; rules, which prevents you from using Yantra bonuses or spell factors:<br /> <a href=\"https://sys.4chan.org/derefer?url=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.4plebs.org%2Ftg%2Fthread%2F47565839%2F%2347571978\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47571978</a><br /> <a href=\"https://sys.4chan.org/derefer?url=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.4plebs.org%2Ftg%2Fthread%2F47565839%2F%2347572307\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47572307</a><br /> <a href=\"https://sys.4chan.org/derefer?url=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.4plebs.org%2Ftg%2Fthread%2F47565839%2F%2347572307\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47572307</a><br /> <a href=\"https://sys.4chan.org/derefer?url=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.4plebs.org%2Ftg%2Fthread%2F47565839%2F%2347578204\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47578204</a><br /> <br /> This does not prevent a mage from repeatedly casting a spell under Praxis in a calm situation to recharge their Mana and Willpower. In other words, with a minutes-long breather lets any mage feast on their own magic and replenish all their Mana and Willpower.<br /> <br /> Something tells me this should probably be added to the errata, because the current errata does not cover it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:26:38-07:00","id":940805,"title":"","content":"Your posts make me seriously wonder what kind of players you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:26:52-07:00","id":940806,"title":"","content":"Simple solution: You only roll dice for casting in a stressful situation. Any spells cast outside that use Down and Dirty Casting. Since no dice are rolled, no successes are exceptional and hence no such lunacy occurs.<br /> <br /> Remember, exceptional successes are only exceptional when the flow of drama says they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:40:54-07:00","id":940820,"title":"","content":"Please don't say things like &quot;you must use.&quot; These games are pretty consistent in saying that if there's something you don't like don't use it. And I personally (as well as the people I play with) find the idea of down and dirty spellcasting both unnecessary and somewhat wrong. When you don't have a time constraint is when you can most easily take the spell factors to the max, which does matter. <br /> <br /> Also, as far as willpower and mana refreshment goes, you really can push your players to be completely empty of both if that is what you are going for (even with praxis being thrown left and right). Some people like that moment of desperation where they're out of common resources and are forced to improvise. Plenty of other people don't. If the maker's of the game (which has been playtested by the way) think that it's perfectly fine to be refreshed of willpower or mana via an exceptional success on a spellcasting roll, and they explicitly design a kind of spell to more easily achieve an exceptional success, I can't believe it didn't cross their minds on how players could get back resources spent in &quot;the field.&quot; It sounds like you simply have a different play style rather than the game needing an errata to change that aspect.<br /> <br /> At least that's my opinion. Take it or leave it as you desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T14:02:31-07:00","id":940837,"title":"","content":"Solution: &quot;hey guys, please don't spam spells for willpower/mana like that.&quot; Or limit that exceptional success benefit to once per scene, in the way that gaining beats from conditions (for example) is limited to once per scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:12:12-07:00","id":940946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=940820#post940820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't say things like &quot;you must use.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Esp. when Dave has never said that. Even in the extremely out of context quotes, he says, &quot;should.&quot; And those links makes it clear that this is a narrative decision, not a &quot;factual&quot; decision based on the game-state.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Additionally, I'd put anything that would be called &quot;spamming,&quot; magic as a 3 dice Wisdom sin, which means characters that want to spam magic are going to have to live with 1-3 Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-31-2016, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T18:30:09-07:00","id":940983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=940946#post940946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Esp. when Dave has never said that. Even in the extremely out of context quotes, he says, &quot;should.&quot; And those links makes it clear that this is a narrative decision, not a &quot;factual&quot; decision based on the game-state.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are not bound by &quot;down and dirty spellcasting,&quot; then you are arguably better off, because then you can employ Yantra bonuses to improve your dice pool and thus make it more likely for you to score an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T18:52:02-07:00","id":940990,"title":"","content":"Well this all sounds really silly.<br /> <br /> Like, how do you go up to your storyteller and tell them you want to cast Speak with the Dead (Death \u2022) until you get all your mana and willpower back.<br /> <br /> If your a storyteller, how would you respond to that? Would you say &quot;yeah, sure Frank, sit here and roll dice for the next 40 minutes while I get a burrito,&quot; or would you say something along the lines of &quot;no?&quot;<br /> <br /> I would say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11660-sleepychicken","name":"SleepyChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11660_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T21:41:13-07:00","id":941030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=940805#post940805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your posts make me seriously wonder what kind of players you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players who follow the rules. A good game includes rules that reward the player for behaving in-character or in-theme. That's why I love WoD's beat system. It rewards players for creating drama. However, it's even more important to eliminate rules which reward the player for behaving out-of-character, since they undo all the effort that was put into the good rules, and then break character on top of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=940837#post940837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solution: &quot;hey guys, please don't spam spells for willpower/mana like that.&quot; Or limit that exceptional success benefit to once per scene, in the way that gaining beats from conditions (for example) is limited to once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exceptional Success benefits limited to one per scene might work, but just saying &quot;don't do that&quot; is completely unreasonable. This is a game about exercising power. Telling people they can't exercise power they logically should be able to is completely inappropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-01-2016, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T22:44:22-07:00","id":941045,"title":"","content":"Why are there &quot;calm situations&quot; in your games? What kind of games are you playing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T23:12:05-07:00","id":941057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Earth Seraph Edna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=940983#post940983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are not bound by &amp;quot;down and dirty spellcasting,&amp;quot; then you are arguably better off, because then you can employ Yantra bonuses to improve your dice pool and thus make it more likely for you to score an exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much the point: if this were real life, every single spell would require time and effort. That effort should be rewarded. Now, the idea of penalizing players because their characters are in a tense, time sensitive situation could be interesting, though if I included such a penalty I personally would first require the players to fail a composure or resolve or composure+resolve check.<br /> <br /> But even still, the others here have the gist of it: players should not be trying to abuse the praxis system, but neither should they be denied the opportunity to cast spells as praxis. This is just common sense. That's exactly the sort of thing that should not be changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T23:39:45-07:00","id":941068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941045#post941045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are there &quot;calm situations&quot; in your games? What kind of games are you playing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea where you're coming from with this comment. How do you manage to play an entire game with no calm moments?<br /> <br /> Take DaveB's Actual Plays for example. Characters often spend weeks going about their lives with no particular threat, or spend a whole session getting sent off to interrogate a ghost or investigate strange graffiti. These are the &quot;calm situations&quot; he's referring to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941057#post941057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much the point: if this were real life, every single spell would require time and effort. That effort should be rewarded. Now, the idea of penalizing players because their characters are in a tense, time sensitive situation could be interesting, though if I included such a penalty I personally would first require the players to fail a composure or resolve or composure+resolve check.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the sentiment that every spell should ostensibly require time and effort, but the rules say that spells can be cast repeatedly at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even still, the others here have the gist of it: players should not be trying to abuse the praxis system, but neither should they be denied the opportunity to cast spells as praxis. This is just common sense. That's exactly the sort of thing that should not be changed. </div> </div> </div>I disagree wholeheartedly. If a player who tries as much as possible to benefit from the praxis system is &quot;abusing&quot; it, then the system should be rewritten or removed.<br /> <br /> Player incentives should lead to a good story, like how the Beat system works. You can't &quot;abuse&quot; the Beat system, because it's well designed. It's totally intended that players try to resolve a condition every scene to gain as much exp as possible. This is how the Praxis system should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-01-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T00:11:51-07:00","id":941077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941068#post941068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree with the sentiment that every spell should ostensibly require time and effort, but the rules say that spells can be cast repeatedly at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> I disagree wholeheartedly. If a player who tries as much as possible to benefit from the praxis system is &amp;quot;abusing&amp;quot; it, then the system should be rewritten or removed.<br /> <br /> Player incentives should lead to a good story, like how the Beat system works. You can't &amp;quot;abuse&amp;quot; the Beat system, because it's well designed. It's totally intended that players try to resolve a condition every scene to gain as much exp as possible. This is how the Praxis system should work.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I speak of time and effort being rewarded, I'm explaining how down and dirty spellcasting doesn't work for me; the very idea that I wouldn't take the time to figure out exactly what my spell is doing is antithetical to my view on spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Also, willpower and mana aren't nearly as abusable as xp beats, so I'd have to say that I disagree with you. Also, I dislike everything having to be spelled out; some things are just better with people understanding that this is a game and that general sportsmanship and friendly conduct simply make for superior gameplay. There are resources to be had, but everything in moderation IS a virtue after all. <br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you are explicitly attempting to showcase the hubris, horror, and alien aspects of mages compared to humans...in which case I would expect you to not have a problem with players easily acquiring plenty of willpower and mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T00:42:01-07:00","id":941085,"title":"","content":"First of all I would note, that the pragraph for down and dirty spellcasting is actually 1/8th of a page, compared to the more than 100 pages for the regular magic rules. And then you should actually read the paragraph again: &quot;Sometimes characters desire to cast spells or create effects that should be easy and require little risk or effort from the mage. Often these spells are effects that the mage creates on a regular basis, and the risk of failure is small and has little to no impact on the drama of the story.&quot;<br /> <br /> The main factor here is not &quot;time constraints&quot; but if the effect of the spell is actually important or not and if the mage is using that kind of spell on a regular basis. The rules are meant to safe time at the table for magic, that is actually not that imporant. If your common sense does not allow you to figure out, when this applies, just don't use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T02:42:53-07:00","id":941112,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> Mana and WP is a pat on the back for rolling an exceptional success and helps relieve some of the narrative burden for the ST in the event that they might have difficulty coming up with a way of describing the effects of the spell being super effective. It's not an excuse to have bad manners at the game table. If you're eating French fries you might offer one to me, but that doesn't mean I then get to take your meal away so I can eat it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T03:33:03-07:00","id":941124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941068#post941068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea where you're coming from with this comment. How do you manage to play an entire game with no calm moments?<br /> Take DaveB's Actual Plays for example. Characters often spend weeks going about their lives with no particular threat, or spend a whole session getting sent off to interrogate a ghost or investigate strange graffiti. These are the &quot;calm situations&quot; he's referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The weeks to which you refer are in fact downtime stretches at the end of which the players would automatically come back with full WP and mana anyway so your argument is useless.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since I know you enjoy overly technical clarification let me explain the metaphor to you that I used in my post just above this one, although inevitably it will break down like all metaphors do. The fry is a spell, the meal is the game. Taking the initiative to ask for a fry (Spell)[Here we'll just have to assume the answer will probably be yes because your dinner partner {That's ST if you're having trouble following along} is a nice guy who wants you to engage in the dinner with him {I hope you remembered that the dinner is the metaphor for the game}], or be given the opportunity to take a fry (Spell) by your dinner guest (ST) is all fine and dandy. Now eating a fry (Spell) is nice, and occassionally you may want to eat more of them (Cast more spells) and bonus they make you feel full (This is the part of the metaphor that relates to getting your WP and mana back by casting spells [Eating fries{Casting spells}]). Just because you enjoy getting full by eating fries (That's getting WP and mana back via casting spells) doesn't mean that you get to steal your dinner parter's (ST) dinner (Game) to eat more fries (Cast more spells). Obviously if you steal the meal (Game) to eat more fries (Cast more spells) then your dinner partner (Your ST) isn't going to get much enjoyment out of his meal (Game). Neither will anyone else at the table (Other players just to make sure you're aware who these mysterious characters I just popped into our dinner [Game] are, they got added in kind of late, I know, whatever). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Everytime you cast a spell you're taking up attention, the ST has to at least glance at your dice results or hear you gloat about succeeding yet again. This is attention that could be better spent running the damn game than watching you roll, roll, roll.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-01-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T05:55:28-07:00","id":941145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941085#post941085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all I would note, that the pragraph for down and dirty spellcasting is actually 1/8th of a page, compared to the more than 100 pages for the regular magic rules. And then you should actually read the paragraph again: &quot;Sometimes characters desire to cast spells or create effects that should be easy and require little risk or effort from the mage. Often these spells are effects that the mage creates on a regular basis, and the risk of failure is small and has little to no impact on the drama of the story.&quot;<br /> <br /> The main factor here is not &quot;time constraints&quot; but if the effect of the spell is actually important or not and if the mage is using that kind of spell on a regular basis. The rules are meant to safe time at the table for magic, that is actually not that imporant. If your common sense does not allow you to figure out, when this applies, just don't use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, characters are arguably more powerful when <b>not</b> constrained by &quot;down and dirty spellcasting,&quot; because it means that they can use Yantra bonuses to more reliably push for success with their Praxis spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T07:50:08-07:00","id":941185,"title":"","content":"Mage functions best when you look at it like this:<br /> Long term mana management is pointless. It hides in every corner of the world, as long as you take care to pick it up. <br /> Mana matters when you don't have time to go looking for it. When a monster chases you. When you are under pressure. Basically, it's like these video games where you start each fight with full health - it's not important that you will get it back before next fight; it's important that it can run out during the scene.<br /> Mana management in Mage matters in context of *scenes*, where characters in general want to achieve a certain goal and they don't have the freedom to spam spells to fully recharge. Like, it's like arguing that Bashing damage is pointless, because it will disappear in an hour or something, so you can walk it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T08:23:56-07:00","id":941205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941185#post941185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage functions best when you look at it like this:<br /> Long term mana management is pointless. It hides in every corner of the world, as long as you take care to pick it up.<br /> Mana matters when you don't have time to go looking for it. When a monster chases you. When you are under pressure. Basically, it's like these video games where you start each fight with full health - it's not important that you will get it back before next fight; it's important that it can run out during the scene.<br /> Mana management in Mage matters in context of *scenes*, where characters in general want to achieve a certain goal and they don't have the freedom to spam spells to fully recharge. Like, it's like arguing that Bashing damage is pointless, because it will disappear in an hour or something, so you can walk it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second that. And I see absolutely no problem with players getting all their mana back if you got some free time. You can even include this narratively and make some kind of meditation out of it to cast the same Praxis over and over again to get enough exeptional successes to fill your mana pool. I wouldn't even let players roll for this if time is not the issue. Just resolve this with something like this: &quot;Gundulf the powerful Magus locked himself up in his fortified bedchamber to meditate on one of his simple Praxis', the perfect recall of a memory. While using this spell for years, he could still glimps the supernal truth whenever he was able to call for a perfect imago of the spell which showed him his dearest memory over and over again. After hours of work he left his bedchamber exhausted, but also empored by the flow of the supernal, which rushed through him.&quot;<br /> And if you don't like that, just houserule, that you only get the benefits of the exeptional succes if the mage casts in a stressful situation. Problem solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:11:51-07:00","id":941360,"title":"","content":"Look at how mana restoration options are designed:<br /> <br /> - Hallow gives you passive mana, yes, but it *also* allows you to <i>literally get mana potions for use in field</i><br /> - Obsessions give you Mana when pushing them forwards, which rewards you for pursuing your Obsession in field so you can squeeze little more Mana in scenes where your Obsession comes in<br /> - Legacy Oblations give you access to Mana when pursuing your Legacy in field, again, allowing you to sustain better while in middle of doing your stuff<br /> - Scouring can be performed right here, right now, giving you <i>a choice between gaining power now and suffering later, allowing you to refuel in middle of the scene at a price of feeling bad later</i><br /> <br /> Have you noticed a pattern? They pretty much want you to <i>go stuff outside of your sanctum and explore, rewarding you for doing so and giving you resources to keep going a little longer. </i> Praxes are no different! They are there to reward you for performing your <i>Signature Magic, so they can reward you for picking a style and sticking to it (which of course creates a pattern, and thus a weakness) while giving you some extra fuel. </i>This game REALLY doesn't want you to go &quot;Ok, dudes, I'm sorry, Mystery Investigation Over, I just had a pretty nasty Paradox twice in a row so I kinda blew all my Mana, sorry, I have to go home eat some Manasandwiches&quot;. It wants you to go &quot;holy mother of mana nugget, I only have 10 points of Mana max, and I need THIS MUCH MANA TO CAST THIS SPELL SAFELY?! HOW WILL I SAVE MYSELF FROM A DEBILITATING CONDITION, TILT OR DEAR EXARCH IN HEAVENS, BEING WOUNDED?!&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T15:54:50-07:00","id":941464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Earth Seraph Edna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941145#post941145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, characters are arguably more powerful when <b>not</b> constrained by &amp;quot;down and dirty spellcasting,&amp;quot; because it means that they can use Yantra bonuses to more reliably push for success with their Praxis spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first off, an exceptional success on a spellcasting roll is only the icing on the cake of properly taking time to cast your spell. The inability to choose exactly what spell factors are being pushed forward and by how much is the truly insulting thing of down and dirty spellcasting. You could completely remove ALL the benefits of exceptional successes on spellcasting and I still would never use the down and dirty rules. Also, most of the time, any intelligent player is going to at least look at the fact that you can add a condition to your character that can turn into a beat so long as you haven't already got a beat from condition resolving in that scene. Beats are in the long run far, far more valuable than a resource that every player should be full of at the start of a chapter (game session). <br /> <br /> Mana and willpower gain in the field from exceptional successes on a spellcasting roll is a feature, NOT a bug. If you don't like that, use a houserule instead of calling for the base game to be changed for your playstyle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T16:15:42-07:00","id":941478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941068#post941068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player incentives should lead to a good story...</div> </div> </div> </div>Player incentives don't lead to good stories, they may facilitate, but they are in no way the measure by which you determine if a story is good or not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:21:28-07:00","id":941608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941124#post941124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The weeks to which you refer are in fact downtime stretches at the end of which the players would automatically come back with full WP and mana anyway so your argument is useless.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since I know you enjoy overly technical clarification let me explain the metaphor to you that I used in my post just above this one, although inevitably it will break down like all metaphors do. The fry is a spell, the meal is the game. Taking the initiative to ask for a fry (Spell)[Here we'll just have to assume the answer will probably be yes because your dinner partner {That's ST if you're having trouble following along} is a nice guy who wants you to engage in the dinner with him {I hope you remembered that the dinner is the metaphor for the game}], or be given the opportunity to take a fry (Spell) by your dinner guest (ST) is all fine and dandy. Now eating a fry (Spell) is nice, and occassionally you may want to eat more of them (Cast more spells) and bonus they make you feel full (This is the part of the metaphor that relates to getting your WP and mana back by casting spells [Eating fries{Casting spells}]). Just because you enjoy getting full by eating fries (That's getting WP and mana back via casting spells) doesn't mean that you get to steal your dinner parter's (ST) dinner (Game) to eat more fries (Cast more spells). Obviously if you steal the meal (Game) to eat more fries (Cast more spells) then your dinner partner (Your ST) isn't going to get much enjoyment out of his meal (Game). Neither will anyone else at the table (Other players just to make sure you're aware who these mysterious characters I just popped into our dinner [Game] are, they got added in kind of late, I know, whatever). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Everytime you cast a spell you're taking up attention, the ST has to at least glance at your dice results or hear you gloat about succeeding yet again. This is attention that could be better spent running the damn game than watching you roll, roll, roll.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I recognize that. It's no fun to have one player hogging all the time and attention. At the same time, I say that that is the game's fault for creating perverse incentives, not the player's for logically following those incentives in a manner consistent with the game's narrative and theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941478#post941478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Player incentives don't lead to good stories, they may facilitate, but they are in no way the measure by which you determine if a story is good or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they determine whether the story is good. I said they affect whether the game itself is good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941077#post941077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I speak of time and effort being rewarded, I'm explaining how down and dirty spellcasting doesn't work for me; the very idea that I wouldn't take the time to figure out exactly what my spell is doing is antithetical to my view on spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Understanding how things work is one of the major themes of the game.<br /> <br /> I read one of DaveB's posts on 4chan, where he acknowledged that Down and Dirty spellcasting changes the player's abilities depending on whether they are in combat and out of combat. He then said that it was also like that in D&amp;D. The thing is, as far as I'm aware, D&amp;D never did that. Maybe he was referring to 4th edition D&amp;D and its &quot;per encounter&quot; powers?<br /> <br /> If he was referring to 4th edition, then I think that's good grounds for houseruling the system away, since &quot;per encounter&quot; powers were one of the things I disliked the most about 4e. The &quot;per encounter&quot; limitation is rooted entirely in game rules, and has no basis in the world and its physics. I find that sort of limitation kills my immersion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, willpower and mana aren't nearly as abusable as xp beats, so I'd have to say that I disagree with you. Also, I dislike everything having to be spelled out; some things are just better with people understanding that this is a game and that general sportsmanship and friendly conduct simply make for superior gameplay. There are resources to be had, but everything in moderation IS a virtue after all.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you are explicitly attempting to showcase the hubris, horror, and alien aspects of mages compared to humans...in which case I would expect you to not have a problem with players easily acquiring plenty of willpower and mana. </div> </div> </div>You disagree with the Beat system and the freedom it provides the player to acquire and resolve conditions?<br /> <br /> In any other RPG, I would agree with your message on good sportsmanship, but not with Mage. Acquiring more power and seeing where it leads you is the name of the game. Rules that make it so that the pursuit of power is &quot;bad sportsmanship&quot; have no place in Mage. Of course you can say things like &quot;That's not fun for us, so stop doing it&quot;, but then you're denying one of the game's main premises. A better solution is: &quot;The storyteller decides the result of an exceptional success&quot; or &quot;You may not choose the same Exceptional Success result more than once per scene&quot;. Now the player character's pursuit of power doesn't mess up anyone else's fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-01-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:41:43-07:00","id":941620,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> The player who abuses the perk is not taking advantage of a perverse incentive, they're being a jerk. It's completely irrational to watch a player abuse the system in such an obvious manner, and hog spotlight time for his spell casting in a way that doesn't benefit the story or the game and then blame the system for the player's bad behavior. Seriously, you're committing victim blaming where the victim is the system.<br /> <br /> And yes, you did say player incentives should lead to good story. Those are your exact words. Rules don't determine the quality of the story, they facilitate the kind of story being told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-01-2016, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:46:04-07:00","id":941621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941360#post941360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at how mana restoration options are designed:<br /> <br /> - Hallow gives you passive mana, yes, but it *also* allows you to <i>literally get mana potions for use in field</i><br /> - Obsessions give you Mana when pushing them forwards, which rewards you for pursuing your Obsession in field so you can squeeze little more Mana in scenes where your Obsession comes in<br /> - Legacy Oblations give you access to Mana when pursuing your Legacy in field, again, allowing you to sustain better while in middle of doing your stuff<br /> - Scouring can be performed right here, right now, giving you <i>a choice between gaining power now and suffering later, allowing you to refuel in middle of the scene at a price of feeling bad later</i><br /> <br /> Have you noticed a pattern? They pretty much want you to <i>go stuff outside of your sanctum and explore, rewarding you for doing so and giving you resources to keep going a little longer. </i> Praxes are no different! They are there to reward you for performing your <i>Signature Magic, so they can reward you for picking a style and sticking to it (which of course creates a pattern, and thus a weakness) while giving you some extra fuel. </i>This game REALLY doesn't want you to go &quot;Ok, dudes, I'm sorry, Mystery Investigation Over, I just had a pretty nasty Paradox twice in a row so I kinda blew all my Mana, sorry, I have to go home eat some Manasandwiches&quot;. It wants you to go &quot;holy mother of mana nugget, I only have 10 points of Mana max, and I need THIS MUCH MANA TO CAST THIS SPELL SAFELY?! HOW WILL I SAVE MYSELF FROM A DEBILITATING CONDITION, TILT OR DEAR EXARCH IN HEAVENS, BEING WOUNDED?!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well Said sir. Motivating players to explore go on adventures and be pro active is good game design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:50:38-07:00","id":941623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941608#post941608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recognize that. It's no fun to have one player hogging all the time and attention. At the same time, I say that that is the game's fault for creating perverse incentives, not the player's for logically following those incentives in a manner consistent with the game's narrative and theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't say they determine whether the story is good. I said they affect whether the game itself is good.<br /> <br /> Absolutely. Understanding how things work is one of the major themes of the game.<br /> <br /> You disagree with the Beat system and the freedom it provides the player to acquire and resolve conditions?<br /> <br /> In any other RPG, I would agree with your message on good sportsmanship, but not with Mage. Acquiring more power and seeing where it leads you is the name of the game. Rules that make it so that the pursuit of power is &quot;bad sportsmanship&quot; have no place in Mage. Of course you can say things like &quot;That's not fun for us, so stop doing it&quot;, but then you're denying one of the game's main premises. A better solution is: &quot;The storyteller decides the result of an exceptional success&quot; or &quot;You may not choose the same Exceptional Success result more than once per scene&quot;. Now the player character's pursuit of power doesn't mess up anyone else's fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not one response you gave makes any sense if you actually read the book as intended like your actually playing the game instead of reading it like a poorly written technical manual similar to Did 4e. Even then your interpretation is damn weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 08-01-2016, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T21:22:36-07:00","id":941670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941608#post941608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You disagree with the Beat system and the freedom it provides the player to acquire and resolve conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Noooo, I believe that limiting the amount of willpower and mana you can get in the field from exceptional successes from spellcasting doesn't make sense unless you are explicitly attempting to force your players to improvise. This in turn means that the benefits of exceptional successes on spellcasting rolls is a case by case thing, not something that should be changed in the base game. I used conditions that grant beats as an example of a much more easily abused resource to showcase that these options are features, not bugs. The fact that you can load up on a ton of conditions as well as the fact that I believe a typical character should be near or at max mana and willpower at the beginning of a chapter were the pieces of evidence I was using to support my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T22:10:11-07:00","id":941690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941620#post941620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> The player who abuses the perk is not taking advantage of a perverse incentive, they're being a jerk. It's completely irrational to watch a player abuse the system in such an obvious manner, and hog spotlight time for his spell casting in a way that doesn't benefit the story or the game and then blame the system for the player's bad behavior. Seriously, you're committing victim blaming where the victim is the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's completely irrational is presenting rules that define a source of power, asking players to role-play a game about acquiring power, and expecting them not to seek the obvious source of power.<br /> <br /> The system can never be a victim. Within the game, the system is omnipotent. It's the system designer's responsibility to avoid the perverse incentives that lead to these situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, you did say player incentives should lead to good story. Those are your exact words. Rules don't determine the quality of the story, they facilitate the kind of story being told. </div> </div> </div>Yes. Player incentives should lead to a good story. In a well-designed system, they do.<br /> <br /> Rules absolutely affect the quality of a story. Poorly designed rules can create plot holes, incentivise characters to violate the game's theme, and ruin dramatic tension when characters overcome obstacles in an unsatisfying way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941670#post941670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noooo, I believe that limiting the amount of willpower and mana you can get in the field from exceptional successes from spellcasting doesn't make sense unless you are explicitly attempting to force your players to improvise. This in turn means that the benefits of exceptional successes on spellcasting rolls is a case by case thing, not something that should be changed in the base game. I used conditions that grant beats as an example of a much more easily abused resource to showcase that these options are features, not bugs. The fact that you can load up on a ton of conditions as well as the fact that I believe a typical character should be near or at max mana and willpower at the beginning of a chapter were the pieces of evidence I was using to support my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course limiting mana gains makes sense, just like how gaining Beats from conditions is limited. With no limit on exceptional successes, mana is never limited in any situation, and that explicitly violates canon, which says that mana is a scarce resource. If you don't change something, then you're creating plot holes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not one response you gave makes any sense if you actually read the book as intended like your actually playing the game instead of reading it like a poorly written technical manual similar to Did 4e. Even then your interpretation is damn weak.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Like I'm actually playing the game?&quot; If I were actually playing the game, and a player demonstrated an unlimited mana engine, I would commend them for it, then devise a houserule to fix the plot hole. If the player came in next game, and demonstrated that the unlimited mana engine was still possible, I would devise a new houserule. If they came in again and it was still possible, then I would go back and fix it again, as many times as necessary. Finding unlimited mana engines is entirely in-theme, in-character and makes perfect sense in the game world, I would absolutely never ever criticize a player for finding one.<br /> <br /> Ideally though, I would come up with the houserules in advance so I don't have to go around changing the rules all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-02-2016, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T23:22:29-07:00","id":941723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941690#post941690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Like I'm actually playing the game?&quot; If I were actually playing the game, and a player demonstrated an unlimited mana engine, I would commend them for it, then devise a houserule to fix the plot hole. If the player came in next game, and demonstrated that the unlimited mana engine was still possible, I would devise a new houserule. If they came in again and it was still possible, then I would go back and fix it again, as many times as necessary. Finding unlimited mana engines is entirely in-theme, in-character and makes perfect sense in the game world, I would absolutely never ever criticize a player for finding one.<br /> <br /> Ideally though, I would come up with the houserules in advance so I don't have to go around changing the rules all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again: nobody but you actually sees a problem with a mana engine if it only works if you got too much free time on your hand. It works in exactly the same narrative sense as if you just say &quot;I use my two days of free time to search for mana.&quot; Only that the latter option is far more interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 08-02-2016, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T23:34:44-07:00","id":941727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941723#post941723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And again: nobody but you actually sees a problem with a mana engine if it only works if you got too much free time on your hand. It works in exactly the same narrative sense as if you just say &quot;I use my two days of free time to search for mana.&quot; Only that the latter option is far more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Too much free time on your hand&quot;? &quot;Taking days to search for mana?&quot; It only takes a few minutes to restore all your mana with a Praxis. If you spend any amount of time not in direct combat, you can restore all your mana well before you reach your next destination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T00:51:12-07:00","id":941759,"title":"","content":"Just limit Willpower and Mana generation from spell Exceptional Success to once per scene - problem solved. My players even more like to get Arcane Beats from Exceptional Success instead of this one.<br /> <br /> Not even pointing that Mind 4 ( or maybe even Mind 3 ) should let you just 'heal' Willpower with spell like Life can heal Health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T02:40:26-07:00","id":941784,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> where did you come by this assumption that mana is supposed to be scarce anyways? Because I can't find any reference to that and in fact in the mana section it says Mages can get Mana from many sources implying it's not scarce at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T02:58:59-07:00","id":941789,"title":"","content":"Tell me, what does this narratively look like? What is the character doing while he refreshes largely mechanical resources?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T03:01:40-07:00","id":941790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941784#post941784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> where did you come by this assumption that mana is supposed to be scarce anyways? Because I can't find any reference to that and in fact in the mana section it says Mages can get Mana from many sources implying it's not scarce at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean scarce in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarcity\" target=\"_blank\">economic sense</a>, i.e. insufficient to meet the unlimited human demand for it. I'm basing it on the fact that it's described in previous books as having monetary value. The fact that mages must resort to so many methods of gathering mana also proves that it's a scarce resource. If there were a way to create unlimited mana engines, you wouldn't need a list of ways to generate mana, you'd simply get it whenever you wanted it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941789#post941789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me, what does this narratively look like? What is the character doing while he refreshes largely mechanical resources?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever he does when he casts spells. Probably concentrating and reciting the same high speech again and again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-02-2016, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T03:20:13-07:00","id":941797,"title":"","content":"Mana isn't scarce. Tass is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T03:21:03-07:00","id":941798,"title":"","content":"Well, given the number of ways that a mage can acquire mana, my group ammended that theme of scarcity to only really applying to three different kinds of mages: novices, outcasts, and idiots. The first two are obvious, the last refers to those that fling vulgar spells around like they're going out of style. And by vulgar I mean spells that risk paradox.<br /> <br /> Oh, sorry, there's a rare fourth category, which is mages that consistently find mysteries that require large mana expenditures to solve. Lucky bastards...lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T03:50:55-07:00","id":941812,"title":"","content":"I saw no mention of mana being exchanged for money either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T04:36:58-07:00","id":941837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941812#post941812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw no mention of mana being exchanged for money either.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the 1e corebook page 389 as part of the Boston setting section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941797#post941797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana isn't scarce. Tass is.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean when you say that Mana isn't scarce?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941798#post941798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, given the number of ways that a mage can acquire mana, my group ammended that theme of scarcity to only really applying to three different kinds of mages: novices, outcasts, and idiots. The first two are obvious, the last refers to those that fling vulgar spells around like they're going out of style. And by vulgar I mean spells that risk paradox.<br /> <br /> Oh, sorry, there's a rare fourth category, which is mages that consistently find mysteries that require large mana expenditures to solve. Lucky bastards...lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only &quot;idiotic&quot; to sink tons of many on mitigating paradox if you can't afford to. With unlimited mana from praxes, that ceases to be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-02-2016, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T04:54:33-07:00","id":941847,"title":"","content":"The 1e corebook is largely defunct with the new edition, there's no reason to suppose that its opinion on the rarity of mana is not also out dated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T04:54:50-07:00","id":941848,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> WHW covered it better than I ever will.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941185#post941185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage functions best when you look at it like this:<br /> Long term mana management is pointless. It hides in every corner of the world, as long as you take care to pick it up.<br /> Mana matters when you don't have time to go looking for it. When a monster chases you. When you are under pressure. Basically, it's like these video games where you start each fight with full health - it's not important that you will get it back before next fight; it's important that it can run out during the scene.<br /> Mana management in Mage matters in context of *scenes*, where characters in general want to achieve a certain goal and they don't have the freedom to spam spells to fully recharge. Like, it's like arguing that Bashing damage is pointless, because it will disappear in an hour or something, so you can walk it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, consider that all Mages start a story with their Mana full. Mana is easy to come by. Emergency reserves? Not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T05:10:24-07:00","id":941858,"title":"","content":"I won't lie, I'm not sure how on-demand refills interact with Focused Mage Sight and spamming mana to gain extra successes when Unpacking A Mystery, but that's because every instinct in my body tells me Unpacking A Mystery isn't designed in a good way anyway. Anyone care to check the consequences for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T05:10:41-07:00","id":941859,"title":"","content":"He'll just complain that they are because you can spam Praxis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T05:39:01-07:00","id":941870,"title":"","content":"Strill is correct, spamming Praxis spells is an easy way to replenish mana, what he fails to realize is that mana scarcity is a defunct part of 1e that was deliberately ignored by the devs. The only real problem with Praxis spamming is that it can be a bit of a dick move by doing something that takes up game time in a way that might not advance the story. Once a player is being a dick it's a table problem and should be settled at the table. If no one cares that a player is spamming his Praxis then it's not a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T05:54:39-07:00","id":941875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941848#post941848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> WHW covered it better than I ever will.<br /> <br /> Plus, consider that all Mages start a story with their Mana full. Mana is easy to come by. Emergency reserves? Not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're completely missing the point. Praxis spam is not only a solution in the long-term, but the short-term as well. Spend a minute or two not occupied with something else, and you're back to full mana. Surely you can acknowledge that that trivializes mana costs in the majority of situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941870#post941870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strill is correct, spamming Praxis spells is an easy way to replenish mana, what he fails to realize is that mana scarcity is a defunct part of 1e that was deliberately ignored by the devs. The only real problem with Praxis spamming is that it can be a bit of a dick move by doing something that takes up game time in a way that might not advance the story. Once a player is being a dick it's a table problem and should be settled at the table. If no one cares that a player is spamming his Praxis then it's not a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>If mana scarcity is defunct, then by definition, mana is unlimited, mana costs have no effect on the game, are completely superfluous, and should be removed as pointless tedium.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's the case. Mana is scarce, and that scarcity creates useful limitations on what you can and cannot do. That's why I continue to insist that praxis spam is a rules flaw which needs to be addressed with houserules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941847#post941847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 1e corebook is largely defunct with the new edition, there's no reason to suppose that its opinion on the rarity of mana is not also out dated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's defunct in terms of mechanics, but it's not been stated exactly what setting aspects are defunct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-02-2016, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:06:09-07:00","id":941882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that's the case. Mana is scarce, and that scarcity creates useful limitations on what you can and cannot do </div> </div> </div>Honestly, like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:07:54-07:00","id":941884,"title":"","content":"The fact that it was omitted from the corebook ought to be implication enough. They didn't write the corebook to tell you how everything is different, they write it so you could play the game. Your inability to grasp this isn't a fault in the system.<br /> <br /> Mana does have some uses, despite the fact that it's not rare you still only have so much of it at a time until you can spam your Praxis. Also, it can do things like slow down your casting via the mana per turn limit if you want to mitigate as much Paradox as possible. That doesn't require mana scarcity in order to function though. Just because it's not as rare as it was doesn't mean it still doesn't have its uses.<br /> <br /> It's like your complaining that salt isn't rare enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-02-2016, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:15:17-07:00","id":941886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941884#post941884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like your complaining that salt isn't rare enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well how else are you supposed to pay soldiers nowadays?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:17:33-07:00","id":941888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941875#post941875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're completely missing the point. Praxis spam is not only a solution in the long-term, but the short-term as well. Spend a minute or two not occupied with something else, and you're back to full mana. Surely you can acknowledge that that trivializes mana costs in the majority of situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, so the players got a moment of relative peace, and for some reason, they're rolling for some trivial stuff just to get their mana back? Follow these steps, then:<br /> <br /> 1st step, is there a chance of success? If no, the action fails. If yes, next step.<br /> 2nd step, is there a chance of failure? If no, the action succeeds. If yes, next step.<br /> 3rd step, is failure interesting? If no, the action succeeds. If yes, roll.<br /> <br /> The real issue here is why the ST is calling for those rolls in the first place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","user":"Justin Sane","date":". 08-02-2016, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:34:05-07:00","id":941928,"title":"","content":"After thinking about this a great deal I\u2019ve come to the conclusion that the only fair way to deal with this mana and willpower refund or the condition that grants beats is to say that it only applies in situations with dramatic tension. <br /> <br /> An example: You have a spell that lets you jump really far. You are out in the middle of nowhere practicing your jump spell. Jump over this, jump over that, but nothing is chasing you. There is no consequence if you fail. If your spell goes well that\u2019s cool but your life didn\u2019t depend on it so you aren\u2019t that PLEASED or REWARDED. There\u2019s no RELEEF of dramatic tension of having overcome a fearful situation. Replenishing will and mana in this case is like a trip to the gas station only you have a gas station everywhere (more on this later).<br /> <br /> Now you are running from a pack of werewolves. They are closing in. You approach a river and your jump spell fails. You splash across but the wolves are faster. They\u2019re gaining on you . . . You reach a cliff with a ledge far above. There\u2019s no time to climb the cliff face but if you make it you think you can lose the werewolf pack. You call up your jump spell, make the leap and find yourself soaring through the air past the ledge you were aiming for all the way to the top of the cliff! The werewolves are ants far below! They are as far below you as you are below the sun! The supernal shines through your elation at surviving! You are so grateful for your powers! You float down to the top of the cliff and catch your breath hearing the frustrated howls of the werewolves far below. You\u2019ve got a huge lead on them now and with any luck you\u2019ll make it out of the woods before they find you again.<br /> Do you see the difference here? In one situation there\u2019s no dramatic tension and thus no corresponding relief if the spell goes well. In the other situation your life depends on the spell working and the exceptional success made the difference between you having to continue running from the werewolves (thus prolonging the scene) and effectively ending the encounter. If I were a storyteller in a mage game that would be my yardstick. There has to be something at risk to reap the benefits from an exceptional success on a spell roll whether that spell is a praxis or not.<br /> <br /> Now let\u2019s take another example: You\u2019re driving your car in the desert. It\u2019s been a while since your last gas station but you\u2019ve still got half a tank. You\u2019re pretty sure you can make it to the next one on the map with some gas to spare. Suddenly some ominous black car starts chasing you. In the ensuing chase you have to race down several side roads or even off road. Through lots of fancy driving you finally get the ominous black car stuck in a ditch. You get back to the road heading toward the next gas station. By the time you get there you\u2019re running on fumes. You pull in only to see that the station is abandoned . . .<br /> <br /> Now here is my two cents on having a repeatable, spam-able, willpower or mana engine. If you are carrying your own gas station with you there is no dramatic tension in seeing the station empty. Your car is always full when it comes to the chase scene and always full afterwards. If you have Life magic hit points are not a problem between encounters. There are specific healing spells in the game, spelled out in the core rules. Therefore the game is designed around replenishing hit points between encounters. This is even truer at higher levels where even aggravated wounds can be healed with extra reach.<br /> <br /> A master of Prime or a master of Spirit with a familiar (essence fountain) won\u2019t have as many problems with mana between encounters. Keep in mind that these are master level spells. Higher level mages should be able to call on more magic. However I don\u2019t see to many spells that flat out heal willpower. Yes you can rip it out of people with Death magic or heal one point a day with the Knit spell (equivalent to a good night\u2019s sleep) but I don\u2019t see any spell that explicitly heals willpower to full from nothing. Taking advantage of critical successes in a literal wording of the rules so that EVERY SPELL heals willpower reliably between encounters with no storyteller input seems to cheapen the other mechanics of replenishing willpower (virtue and vice, rest ect). This is another reason that if I were storytelling a game I would only allow critical successes on spells to replenish willpower and mana if that critical success helped resolve a stressful encounter. <br /> <br /> The essence fountain \u201cmana engine\u201d or the ability to create permanent hallows as a master of Prime are the equivalent of having a solar powered car (essence fountain) or a solar powered house (lasting create truth). Both have their uses, both have their limits, neither spell replenishes willpower.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:43:55-07:00","id":941937,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, no that's not the only fair way to deal with the &quot;problem.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:57:29-07:00","id":941943,"title":"","content":"I don't like making Praxes work only during INTENSE DRAMATIC LIFE DEPENDING SCENES, mostly because for cost of 4 praxes, you could just get a new dot of Arcana. You buy them for a reason, this reason being &quot;exceptional success&quot;, and taking that away seems like creating a trap buy.<br /> Most of Mana Engines can be accessed by starting characters, btw. There is a Mind Spell at 3rd dots that restores you one willpower per use, and Life 3 has a spell that gives you benefits of a nights rest - night rest restores 1 willpower too.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Again, note that Full Refill on Willpower isn't as good for Mages as it is for other splats. Mages BURN willpower. Math is so stacked that you are going to spend Willpower on pretty much every single Mage-specific ability in order to have decent chance of success. For starting Mages, Willpower is A MUST to reliably cast anything past parlor trick. 2 or 3 rounds of combat can burn off a &quot;Willpower 6&quot; Mage from 100 to 0, especially if it involves Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-02-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:05:50-07:00","id":941950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941943#post941943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of Mana Engines can be accessed by starting characters, btw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Drain a Hallow, Shift some Sands back to when it was full, repeat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:20:59-07:00","id":941962,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow off-screen spamming of Praxis for WP and Mana for the same reason I wouldn't allow off-screen spamming of skills for Conditions. It doesn't need to be intensely dramatic, but it does need to be interesting enough to justify it happening during a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:24:54-07:00","id":941964,"title":"","content":"2nd edition Mage is all about creativity and you should treat all of the spells as examples. So if Life can heal body, Spirit and Death can heal ephemera it means that Mind can heal Willpower and writing it in corebook is just a waste of paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:28:15-07:00","id":941965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941962#post941962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow off-screen spamming of Praxis for WP and Mana for the same reason I wouldn't allow off-screen spamming of skills for Conditions. It doesn't need to be intensely dramatic, but it does need to be interesting enough to justify it happening during a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually do this. People who engage in a skill a lot get an Equipment Bonus for it. For example, a Pro Boxer who trains a lot gets Brawling Equipment [Box Training] tied to a [Boxin Champ] condition. <br /> This was our solution to a problem of &quot;how to make a Pro different from a Newbie when they both have same skill dots&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:28:51-07:00","id":941966,"title":"","content":"At WHW: I acknowledge that a nights rest restores a point of willpower but its only one per day. That's why I would think Knit with reach only works once per day. With the Mind 3 spell do you mean Augment Mind? So if a mind mage augments someone's composure or resolve for a scene and that boost's willpower does the subject keep that willpower after the augmenting spell expires? If so then yes you have a willpower engine, but you need more magic to use it and can only use it once per scene. If the subject only has the extra willpower while the augmenting spell lasts then you have to track the phantom willpower points separately and have a time limit on when they can be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:33:44-07:00","id":941967,"title":"","content":"No, I mean Clear Thoughts, which has a Reach for restoring Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:38:36-07:00","id":941970,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3741\" data-vbnamecard=\"3741\">Servanous</a> Do not limit yourself to the spells that are in a book. Willpower can be restored with Mind Perfecting spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:54:39-07:00","id":941984,"title":"","content":"At WHW thanks for pointing that out, that makes Mind mages more valuable to the group. What I'm looking for is consistency. I don't like loopholes in rules that can be exploited by metagaming players at the expense of in character intelligence. I want rules that are useable by the players and their opponents equally, so the game comes down to storytelling rather than rules lawyering. The most frustrating game I ever played was where my character got killed by a sneak attack of death that by base rules could not have happened. I learned later that there was an exception made specifically for that opponent and was not to be used outside that story module and never by the player characters. I left that game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:58:44-07:00","id":941985,"title":"","content":"A poultry farm, Devouring the Slain, and some spell Factors on Scale and you should be full as well with a single casting. Depending on how you read the Wisdom section that might count as an act of hubris, so you depending on ST you might have to inure that spell. You will need to spend enough Reach that you'll risk Paradox anyway (instant, sensory, affecting healthy targets, not count against Mana scouring Limit). Add Space 2 and a good link to the farm and you can do that anytime and from anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:08:28-07:00","id":941993,"title":"","content":"Talking about Devouring The Slain, with new Paradox Releasing, I can't stop but think about THE CHICKEN APOCALYPSE of ZOMBIE CHICKENS that got corrupted by &quot;apply a Condition to the Subject&quot; option on the Paradox Table.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you could just nab Rank 1 Ghosts and explode them with DvSlain, it's not like they are self aware or truly intelligent anyway. With a Ghost Familiar, you could just rough it up, then heal it with Quicken Ghost, and repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:34:22-07:00","id":942014,"title":"","content":"Depending on how you rule, there is another option to recharging mana/willpower, and that is Time 3 Temporal Summoning to instantly bring you back to full mana and willpower. Of course, this brings into a lot of possibilities such as your mind being reset to the restored version meaning you would have no idea what you were doing originally, but from reading the book it is heavily implied you keep your current state of mind because honestly it would be quite interesting to flux back and forth by summoning an earlier version of yourself, then trying to figure out what is happening before reverting back to normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:12:03-07:00","id":942094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941886#post941886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well how else are you supposed to pay soldiers nowadays?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a history nerd I appreciate this joke","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:14:23-07:00","id":942143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941962#post941962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow off-screen spamming of Praxis for WP and Mana for the same reason I wouldn't allow off-screen spamming of skills for Conditions. It doesn't need to be intensely dramatic, but it does need to be interesting enough to justify it happening during a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yes.<br /> <br /> Look, a starting character can be taken down by about six or seven housecats all attacking them at the same time. Is this going to happen in real life? No, though kitty might claw a good bit. Just because there's a hole or exploit in the system doesn't mean it's broken or a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:49:59-07:00","id":942171,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but saying &quot;just because it's flawed doesn't mean it's flawed&quot; makes me laugh, and not in a good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:19:18-07:00","id":942192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=942171#post942171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but saying &quot;just because it's flawed doesn't mean it's flawed&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't happen.<br /> <br /> &quot;Failing to run this narrative-building game as a narrative-building game by allowing players to do things that serve no narrative-building purpose and only engage with the rules of the game outside of that context is not a sign that the game is bad at being a narrative-building game just because you made the decision to try and run it as a simulation of reality or a strictly mechanical exercise&quot; is not &quot;just because it's flawed doesn't mean it's flawed.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:22:36-07:00","id":942194,"title":"","content":"It's all fun-and-games until some smart-ass Thyrsus decides to turn a nearby flock of pigeons into cats and has them maul that Seer to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T23:55:30-07:00","id":942540,"title":"","content":"Actually if you influence 20 housecats to viciously attack a single human and claw him to death, that might pretty much work. It's simply that that will never happen naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T04:26:56-07:00","id":942632,"title":"","content":"Here is how quickly you can run out of Willpower in a stressful situation [1 round]<br /> 1. You want your spell to succeed; you can't spend additional turns adding yantras, so you add the biggest one reflexively, and burn a WIllpower point to get sweet +3 to the roll so you have a decent chance of succeeding. [WP spent: 1]<br /> 2. You lacked Reach to do it safely, so you decided to make a gamble and Throw the Spell; you roll Gnosis+Athletics, and because of Defense/Penalties/Whatever, you Willpower to get +3 to it so you won't miss [WP spent: 2]<br /> 3. Some asshole decided to Counterspell your spell! You Clash of Will. Dude Willpowered his roll, so you need to match the stakes, and willpower too [WP spent: 3]<br /> 4. Annoyingly enough, there is some kind of effect that interferes with your spell, and you need to beat it in Clash of Will to get it going. Again, Willpower to rescue [WP spent: 4]<br /> 5. And even after everything, Jerk#2 casts a spell at you which you Withstand, and you really need to survive it, so you Willpower to get +2 Withstand rating [WP spent: 5]<br /> 6. Oh, and if any of the Jerks decides to contest some of your Shielding spells that operate on Clash of Will, prepare yourself to Willpower away [WP spent: 5+]<br /> <br /> Is it a white room scenario? Kinda. But chances are, in high risk high tension situations, at least some parts of it will come into play. The fact that your Mage can burn through 3 points of Willpower just to make sure his spell works can be nuts.<br /> *And yes, I'm assuming that you can spend multiple Willpower points per round, but only one per action, as more than one 2nd ED book claims so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T04:42:43-07:00","id":942636,"title":"","content":"I was tidying up my house rules when I figured out one that might help for those situations when you want your players not to spam stuff (normally, just telling them not to do it is enough, but yeah, this might help &quot;gameist&quot; types).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Repeated Spells </span></span></b></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">When casting a spell that the mage had already failed to cast during that scene, the mage gets a cumulative (for that spell only) -1 die penalty to her spellcasting pool (so far this is the basic CoD rule). On top of that, if the spell did not normally risk any Paradox, now it risks 1 die of Paradox. The mage must use different Yantra on the new attempt or it automatically fails. This spell grants no extra benefits on an Exceptional Success. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T05:01:23-07:00","id":942641,"title":"","content":"To me, there is nothing wrong with this rule. I mean who cares if you can get full mana and full willpower from spamming Praxis, let it happen and off screen if you must. If the player insists on doing this in combat and it is becoming rather annoying, then just remove them from the conflict in some fashion. I mean, if you are spamming spells that are useless to a fight, then your character is pretty much open for attack and definitely an easy target. If the other characters protect him while he is doing this, then it is an effective strategy. I don't see the harm in this at all, unless it is disruptive to the fun everyone is enjoying. You could always say a Sleeper walked in if they started spamming spells and let the Paradox handle the situation.<br /> <br /> Also, as it has been stated many times before, there are plenty of mana batteries that exist doing different things, so apparently mana is suppose to be easily attained and some of them without a risk of Wisdom sin. I think in 1E that was something that people were scrounging for Hallows and artifacts since those were 2 heavily reliable sources of continuous mana, but in 2E there are so many sources they removed the mana regeneration of artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 08-03-2016, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:00:28-07:00","id":943249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941882#post941882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, like?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't use all flavors of mage sight on everything. You can't dump tons of mana into mitigating paradox at every convenience. You can't spam powerful spells like Shifting Sands at every convenience. You have to spend around at least an hour or so to recover any mana you spent frivolously, and there's the chance that you might well run out of ways to recover mana until the following day.<br /> <br /> It also means you're incentivized to use your legacy oblation to regain mana, which provides interesting thematic flavor and story hook possibilities. If you leave praxis spam, then all other forms of mana recovery are obsolete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941888#post941888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, so the players got a moment of relative peace, and for some reason, they're rolling for some trivial stuff just to get their mana back? Follow these steps, then:<br /> <br /> 1st step, is there a chance of success? If no, the action fails. If yes, next step.<br /> 2nd step, is there a chance of failure? If no, the action succeeds. If yes, next step.<br /> 3rd step, is failure interesting? If no, the action succeeds. If yes, roll.<br /> <br /> The real issue here is why the ST is calling for those rolls in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not trivial. Discovering an unlimited mana engine is a fascinating mystery that any mage should seek out. That's the fundamental problem here. By every metric, mages SHOULD be spamming praxes to recover mana. It fits in setting because praxes are spells that you've practiced by casting repeatedly. It fits in theme because discovering a complication-free unlimited mana engine is a monumental accomplishment. It fits in character because your character should be fascinated by this.<br /> <br /> It fits in every way except that it's not fun. It takes interesting methods of mana recovery, like Legacy oblations, and renders them obsolete. It allows mages to recover mana on a much smaller timescale than any other reliable method of mana recovery. That's why I insist that it's a rules problem, and not a player problem. The player has every reason and justification to do it. It's the system that can't handle it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941928#post941928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A master of Prime or a master of Spirit with a familiar (essence fountain) won\u2019t have as many problems with mana between encounters. Keep in mind that these are master level spells. Higher level mages should be able to call on more magic. However I don\u2019t see to many spells that flat out heal willpower. Yes you can rip it out of people with Death magic or heal one point a day with the Knit spell (equivalent to a good night\u2019s sleep) but I don\u2019t see any spell that explicitly heals willpower to full from nothing. Taking advantage of critical successes in a literal wording of the rules so that EVERY SPELL heals willpower reliably between encounters with no storyteller input seems to cheapen the other mechanics of replenishing willpower (virtue and vice, rest ect). This is another reason that if I were storytelling a game I would only allow critical successes on spells to replenish willpower and mana if that critical success helped resolve a stressful encounter.<br /> <br /> The essence fountain \u201cmana engine\u201d or the ability to create permanent hallows as a master of Prime are the equivalent of having a solar powered car (essence fountain) or a solar powered house (lasting create truth). Both have their uses, both have their limits, neither spell replenishes willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true. A Master of Prime will absolutely NOT always be at full mana. Creating Hallows has widespread repercussions to the surrounding area, and is highly likely to be regulated by the local concilium. Furthermore, even if you have a few powerful hallows, you certainly aren't going to be able to run back to them between every scene to top yourself off. You'll have to manage with what you have. That's why I'm ok with this form of mana engine.<br /> <br /> A master of Spirit, on the other hand, has no such restrictions. They can recover all their mana at any time, in only a few seconds.<br /> <br /> I absolutely agree with your assessment on Willpower. Unlimited willpower ruins the Virtue and Vice systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=941962#post941962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow off-screen spamming of Praxis for WP and Mana for the same reason I wouldn't allow off-screen spamming of skills for Conditions. It doesn't need to be intensely dramatic, but it does need to be interesting enough to justify it happening during a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't accept this unless there's an in-universe justification for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=942143#post942143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much, yes.<br /> <br /> Look, a starting character can be taken down by about six or seven housecats all attacking them at the same time. Is this going to happen in real life? No, though kitty might claw a good bit. Just because there's a hole or exploit in the system doesn't mean it's broken or a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it'll happen. That's basically what Alfred Hitchcock's <i>The Birds</i> is about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=942192#post942192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't happen.<br /> <br /> &quot;Failing to run this narrative-building game as a narrative-building game by allowing players to do things that serve no narrative-building purpose and only engage with the rules of the game outside of that context is not a sign that the game is bad at being a narrative-building game just because you made the decision to try and run it as a simulation of reality or a strictly mechanical exercise&quot; is not &quot;just because it's flawed doesn't mean it's flawed.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes no sense. Mage is a game about understanding the universe. Engaging with the rules of the game outside of a narrative context is exactly what mages set out to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=942632#post942632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is how quickly you can run out of Willpower in a stressful situation [1 round]<br /> 1. You want your spell to succeed; you can't spend additional turns adding yantras, so you add the biggest one reflexively, and burn a WIllpower point to get sweet +3 to the roll so you have a decent chance of succeeding. [WP spent: 1]<br /> 2. You lacked Reach to do it safely, so you decided to make a gamble and Throw the Spell; you roll Gnosis+Athletics, and because of Defense/Penalties/Whatever, you Willpower to get +3 to it so you won't miss [WP spent: 2]<br /> 3. Some asshole decided to Counterspell your spell! You Clash of Will. Dude Willpowered his roll, so you need to match the stakes, and willpower too [WP spent: 3]<br /> 4. Annoyingly enough, there is some kind of effect that interferes with your spell, and you need to beat it in Clash of Will to get it going. Again, Willpower to rescue [WP spent: 4]<br /> 5. And even after everything, Jerk#2 casts a spell at you which you Withstand, and you really need to survive it, so you Willpower to get +2 Withstand rating [WP spent: 5]<br /> 6. Oh, and if any of the Jerks decides to contest some of your Shielding spells that operate on Clash of Will, prepare yourself to Willpower away [WP spent: 5+]<br /> <br /> Is it a white room scenario? Kinda. But chances are, in high risk high tension situations, at least some parts of it will come into play. The fact that your Mage can burn through 3 points of Willpower just to make sure his spell works can be nuts.<br /> *And yes, I'm assuming that you can spend multiple Willpower points per round, but only one per action, as more than one 2nd ED book claims so.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still doesn't justify making willpower nigh-unlimited via recovery spells. It renders the virtue and vice systems obsolete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=942641#post942641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, there is nothing wrong with this rule. I mean who cares if you can get full mana and full willpower from spamming Praxis, let it happen and off screen if you must. If the player insists on doing this in combat and it is becoming rather annoying, then just remove them from the conflict in some fashion. I mean, if you are spamming spells that are useless to a fight, then your character is pretty much open for attack and definitely an easy target. If the other characters protect him while he is doing this, then it is an effective strategy. I don't see the harm in this at all, unless it is disruptive to the fun everyone is enjoying. You could always say a Sleeper walked in if they started spamming spells and let the Paradox handle the situation.<br /> <br /> Also, as it has been stated many times before, there are plenty of mana batteries that exist doing different things, so apparently mana is suppose to be easily attained and some of them without a risk of Wisdom sin. I think in 1E that was something that people were scrounging for Hallows and artifacts since those were 2 heavily reliable sources of continuous mana, but in 2E there are so many sources they removed the mana regeneration of artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>In World of Darkness games, each splat gets a fuel stat. In each game, the purpose of that fuel stat is, in part, to ensure that the character must act like a monster in order to use their abilities. For example, a Vampire must drink peoples' blood in order to activate their disciplines. A Changeling must manipulate people's emotions like a True Fae in order to restore Glamour.<br /> <br /> In Mage, the theme is less clear because there are lots of different ways to get mana, but where it is clear is in Legacy Oblations. Legacies are what truly take a mage from human to monster, because they are capable of rewriting the mage's nature and morality. Therefore, performing Legacy Oblations to regain mana is a key thematic aspect that emphasizes their inhuman nature.<br /> <br /> However, if you allow praxis spam, you render every other method of mana recovery completely obsolete. Throw out Hallows, you can't take them with you, and they take an hour to do an oblation in. Throw out Pattern Scouring, it costs you HP. Throw out Legacy oblations, they take too long. In fact, you might as well remove the whole mana system entirely, because there's very little chance that you'll actually run out of mana before you get a chance to recover it.<br /> <br /> Allowing praxis spam is tantamount to gutting the whole mana system and everything it adds to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-03-2016, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:12:02-07:00","id":943372,"title":"","content":"Mages are not Bugs fucking Bunny. They cannot engage with the game rules outside of a narrative context because that world does not exist. It's not even something that lies in beyond the Lie, or in the Empyrean. It's not even non-existant in the way Atlantis is. Mage is not Toon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:40:36-07:00","id":943387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943372#post943372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are not Bugs fucking Bunny. They cannot engage with the game rules outside of a narrative context because that world does not exist. It's not even something that lies in beyond the Lie, or in the Empyrean. It's not even non-existant in the way Atlantis is. Mage is not Toon.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that it is possible for a character to understand the game world. That's a core premise of the game - exploring mysteries. For it to be possible to understand the game world, the laws governing the world must not be completely arbitrary and random. Therefore, if a player character discovers some seeming inconsistency, there must be an in-universe reason for it. It then becomes a mystery for them to solve, and the source of a new plot hook.<br /> <br /> Therefore I don't accept that a mage gains mana from praxes only when it is narratively convenient, just because the Storyteller says so. That in itself is a perfectly valid mystery. Therefore there should either be an in-universe explanation, or otherwise the idea should be abandoned as a flagrant plot hole and red herring. Otherwise it just serves to highlight the fourth wall and distract from the story proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-04-2016, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:54:13-07:00","id":943396,"title":"","content":"I think you understand the word &quot;understand&quot; in a context that isn't accurate for what mages do. They understand it in the way a Taoists understands the Eternal Tao-that which can be named is not the Eternal Tao. It is not knowing, it is becoming. The Chronicles world is fundamentally unknowable-but it can be transcended into.<br /> <br /> More on point, a) in universe, you are still arguing that a mage can interact with something that literally does not exist for them, because game mechanics are an abstraction used by the players benefits to arbitrate the world willed into being by the players, and b) while it's ultimately the group's decision, the group's decision also includes the decision to allow the Storyteller to be the final arbiter on things, so The Storyteller says so&quot; is just about literally is the end all, be all of declarations.<br /> <br /> What is proposed is cartoonish, which is literally the most singularly most story-distracting, fourth-wall leaning adjectival-thing that can be done in this game. It also belies a poor understanding of how games works.<br /> <br /> So, go ahead, don't accept it. You are free to be wrong at your own table. But you are wrong in the shared context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:13:12-07:00","id":943410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943396#post943396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you understand the word &quot;understand&quot; in a context that isn't accurate for what mages do. They understand it in the way a Taoists understands the Eternal Tao-that which can be named is not the Eternal Tao. It is not knowing, it is becoming. The Chronicles world is fundamentally unknowable-but it can be transcended into.<br /> <br /> More on point, a) in universe, you are still arguing that a mage can interact with something that literally does not exist for them, because game mechanics are an abstraction used by the players benefits to arbitrate the world willed into being by the players, and b) while it's ultimately the group's decision, the group's decision also includes the decision to allow the Storyteller to be the final arbiter on things, so The Storyteller says so&quot; is just about literally is the end all, be all of declarations.<br /> <br /> What is proposed is cartoonish, which is literally the most singularly most story-distracting, fourth-wall leaning adjectival-thing that can be done in this game. It also belies a poor understanding of how games works.<br /> <br /> So, go ahead, don't accept it. You are free to be wrong at your own table. But you are wrong in the shared context.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not cartoonish. The book itself says that a character acquires a praxis in-universe by casting it over and over again. It should be perfectly natural for a mage to continue doing this on a regular basis. Furthermore, mages absolutely CAN interact with exceptional successes. Exceptional successes are an aspect of Fate. Any mage with Fate can observe, study, and manipulate them. Even without Fate, a mage can tell that they've gained mana from casting the spell, and connect the dots. Therefore, there's no reason why a mage shouldn't be able to study exceptional successes in-depth and determine that they're an untapped source of mana.<br /> <br /> If you were talking about a Storyteller saying &quot;No you can't just blow up a city block for no reason. Come up with a better character motivation&quot;, then I'd absolutely agree with you. However, in this case, praxis spam constitutes a completely valid mystery to study. The problem that it breaks canon and ruins the mana economy is the fault of the system, not of the player who found a perfectly valid in-character goal. That's why I say it should be houseruled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-04-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:22:20-07:00","id":943414,"title":"","content":"You are literally suggesting that a character do something he has no reason to do except for the fact that it can be done as a result of forces that exist beyond the screen.You are suggesting that a character is expected to put their hands on the knobs of the tv screen and futz around with them.<br /> <br /> Mages are not Bugs fucking Bunny. There are no mechanics from the mage's perspective. There is the world.<br /> <br /> You are wrong in the shared context.<br /> <br /> More on point, if you disagree, why not go see what your own group says about it. Because if they agree with you, who the fuck cares. We don't sit at your table.<br /> <br /> If you tried it at my table, I would say you were gaming in bad faith, and if you kept pushing the matter, I'd either ask you to leave the table or accept that the universe does not respond kindly in game and proceed to deliver karma.<br /> <br /> Without a table, it's very clear that what you propose goes against the spirit and faith of the game as presented by the book, possible mechanical interpretations in one small section be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:43:01-07:00","id":943423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943414#post943414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are literally suggesting that a character do something he has no reason to do except for the fact that it can be done as a result of forces that exist beyond the screen.You are suggesting that a character is expected to put their hands on the knobs of the tv screen and futz around with them.<br /> <br /> Mages are not Bugs fucking Bunny. There are no mechanics from the mage's perspective. There is the world.<br /> <br /> You are wrong in the shared context.<br /> <br /> More on point, if you disagree, why not go see what your own group says about it. Because if they agree with you, who the fuck cares. We don't sit at your table.<br /> <br /> If you tried it at my table, I would say you were gaming in bad faith, and if you kept pushing the matter, I'd either ask you to leave the table or accept that the universe does not respond kindly in game and proceed to deliver karma.<br /> <br /> Without a table, it's very clear that what you propose goes against the spirit and faith of the game as presented by the book, possible mechanical interpretations in one small section be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! The mage doesn't see mechanics, he sees the world! That's my point! Everything you need to justify praxis spam can be explained entirely in-world. The mage casts his praxis twice during a fight, and each time he feels a euphoric rush, and notes that he's ended up with more mana than he started. When he gets home that evening and practices his praxis as usual, he studies himself with mage sight. After a few tries, he sees the threads of Fate converge while he experiences that same euphoric rush, and finds that he once again ends his session with more mana than he started. He then proceeds to study this phenomenon in-depth, trying to replicate his previous results, and discovers that convergences of exceptionally good luck interwoven with supernal magic, are an untapped source of mana.<br /> <br /> Which would be all well and good except for the fact that it all violates canon. Why hasn't anyone else done the same thing before? Why hasn't it rendered all other sources of mana obsolete?<br /> <br /> That is why I say it's a rules problem. Everything the player did is perfectly reasonable in-character, but it didn't fit with the setting. That's a plot hole in the setting, not the fault of the player.<br /> <br /> If the Storyteller just says &quot;don't do that&quot;, they're essentially saying that exceptional successes are part of the fourth wall, which they are not. Exceptional successes are an in-character part of the world which characters should be able to study. What happens if an exceptional success is a key clue in a mystery? Do you also complain about a player who refers to an exceptional success in-character? By tossing exceptional successes across the fourth wall, you're rewriting Fate's purview!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T02:04:54-07:00","id":943493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943249#post943249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I insist that it's a rules problem, and not a player problem. The player has every reason and justification to do it. It's the system that can't handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>False dichotomy. If a player knows the system can't handle a situation, and keeps pushing towards it, even after being asked to stop? It's not just a rules problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943423#post943423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He then proceeds to study this phenomenon in-depth, trying to replicate his previous results, and discovers that convergences of exceptionally good luck interwoven with supernal magic, are an untapped source of mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, since this is likely a downtime action, no dice are rolled, and while the Mage still adquires quite a bit of practice, he just doesn't feel the rush he felt back then.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:14:35-07:00","id":943512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943493#post943493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">False dichotomy. If a player knows the system can't handle a situation, and keeps pushing towards it, even after being asked to stop? It's not just a rules problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think it's better to dance around and ignore plot holes, rather than take the simple steps needed to fix them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively, since this is likely a downtime action, no dice are rolled, and while the Mage still adquires quite a bit of practice, he just doesn't feel the rush he felt back then. </div> </div> </div>Then this requires an in-setting explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:19:17-07:00","id":943514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943512#post943512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you think it's better to dance around and ignore plot holes, rather than take the simple steps needed to fix them?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, holes should be fixed. However, if that's not possible, and someone keeps finding new and interesting ways to fall into them, even after all the warning signs were posted... Then maybe, just <i>maybe</i>, the person jumping into it is as big a problem as the hole itself.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then this requires an in-setting explanation. </div> </div> </div>It's a Mystery.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:28:38-07:00","id":943519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943514#post943514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, holes should be fixed. However, if that's not possible, and someone keeps finding new and interesting ways to fall into them, even after all the warning signs were posted... Then maybe, just <i>maybe</i>, the person jumping into it is as big a problem as the hole itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the player jumping in them can justify what they're doing within the narrative, and if it fits the game's themes and premise, then they're completely entitled to do that.<br /> <br /> There shouldn't be warning signs because it's a perfectly reasonable thing to investigate. Just solve the problem with a quick houserule and be done with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a Mystery. </div> </div> </div>Firstly, it's not. Exceptional Successes are a basic thing you can observe with Fate. To say that they're unknown to mages is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Second, even if we assume that it's a mystery, every mystery has an answer. What answer will the mage find when they study this phenomenon with Fate sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-04-2016, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:20:10-07:00","id":943534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943519#post943519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the player jumping in them can justify what they're doing within the narrative, and if it fits the game's themes and premise, then they're completely entitled to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey guys, there's this flaw with the system, please do your best to ignore it, okay? Suspension of disbelief and all that.&quot;<br /> &quot;But it's in the system! I'm entitled to it!&quot;<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Firstly, it's not. Exceptional Successes are a basic thing you can observe with Fate. To say that they're unknown to mages is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Second, even if we assume that it's a mystery, every mystery has an answer. What answer will the mage find when they study this phenomenon with Fate sight? </div> </div> </div>Fate likes drama. Practicing isn't dramatic enough for Fate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:52:42-07:00","id":943544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943512#post943512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then this requires an in-setting explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. First off my first thought on the practice or repetitive casting was not &quot;the mages sits in their room and spams the spell over and over for no reason other than gaining a praxis&quot; but &quot;the mages uses this spell so frequently that it's pretty much part of their day to day job or similar&quot;. Like mortician with Forensic Gaze or a burglar with Without a Trace.<br /> <br /> The exceptional success to me represents a moment where the imago lines up perfectly with Supernal ideals relevant to the current situation (which is why it's still not a guaranteed exceptional success) giving the mage an &quot;Aha!&quot; moment. It's a moment of insight that allows the mage to get a little extra.<br /> <br /> The mage who sits in their room spamming a spell gets no exceptional successes because theirs no variation. There's nothing to go &quot;Aha!&quot; over. The guy working in the worryingly busy morgue who examines one or two corpses a day gets plenty such moments with forensic gaze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil","name":"Kamikazegerbil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1571_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:45:45-07:00","id":943563,"title":"","content":"I would think exceptional successes would also need to be something resolving around some type of conflict, whether internal or external.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 08-04-2016, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:22:07-07:00","id":943636,"title":"","content":"As a ST, I would use the situation to define what differentiates an exceptional success from a regular success.<br /> <br /> Much like the way one of those other systems use the concept of Taking 10 or Taking 20, if there is no possibility of negative consequences, then it is just a normal success.<br /> <br /> Casting a spell over and over, in a multitude of situations and conditions allows a mage to master the spell, and thus allows it to become a praxis. This makes is easier for the mage to gain an exceptional success when casting this spell.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical point, limiting exceptional successes to actions that pose the potential for bad things to happen to you if you fail allows for a consistent rule that players can follow while also keeping its value for bonuses when they count. If failure doesn't count in the practice room where you are practicing, then exceptional successes don't count either.<br /> <br /> From a narrative or thematic point, limiting exceptional successes to spells cast &quot;In Play&quot; (I don't count the practice spam room as in play) maintains the tension between risk and reward.<br /> <br /> I do not agree that an exceptional success is a thing within the game universe, or that it is something that can be monitored, managed, and replicated using Fate. Fate in my mind can be used to increase your odds to such a degree that it is more likely that your mage will achieve spectacular results. But unless your mage is actually rolling dice that truly determine the outcome of his actions, the concept of an exceptional success is purely mechanical and removed from the view and manipulation of the character.<br /> <br /> So this means praxis spaming will not be a thing in my games. Any attempts at such will meet with Mr. Paradox (Cousin to Mr. Murphy) in some way, shape, form, or fashion.<br /> <br /> For anyone asking, or even demanding, an in-universe explanation, I would answer that Fate is fickle, unpredictable, and inscrutable. Even for mages. At least those below 8 or so dots in the Fate arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:42:43-07:00","id":943836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943519#post943519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, even if we assume that it's a mystery, every mystery has an answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Patently not true, especially in a role-playing game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:49:24-07:00","id":943900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943636#post943636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But unless your mage is actually rolling dice that truly determine the outcome of his actions, the concept of an exceptional success is purely mechanical and removed from the view and manipulation of the character.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> This. And if you don't like it, just use the houserule that praxis only give mana back during scenes of tension with all other exceptional success options unchanged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T00:11:20-07:00","id":944168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943636#post943636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not agree that an exceptional success is a thing within the game universe, or that it is something that can be monitored, managed, and replicated using Fate. Fate in my mind can be used to increase your odds to such a degree that it is more likely that your mage will achieve spectacular results. But unless your mage is actually rolling dice that truly determine the outcome of his actions, the concept of an exceptional success is purely mechanical and removed from the view and manipulation of the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a matter of my personal opinion. The book says so. p. 91: &quot;Fate Sight highlights anyone the mage watches who experiences a dramatic failure or exceptional success.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For anyone asking, or even demanding, an in-universe explanation, I would answer that Fate is fickle, unpredictable, and inscrutable. Even for mages. At least those below 8 or so dots in the Fate arcana. </div> </div> </div>That works, at least to some extent. If you take this to its logical extreme, however, then destinies don't exist because Fate is too fickle and inscrutible to decide on a coherent destiny.<br /> <br /> Fate obviously does have a rhyme and a reason, but one too complex for mortals to fully comprehend. You can tell that by the fact that concepts like &quot;luck&quot; and &quot;destiny&quot; exist. Their reasons aren't clear, but they nevertheless still represent a pattern in Fate that can be identified. I would therefore clarify this idea by saying that Fate's behavior can be observed, and some patterns to its actions can be discerned, but not enough to predict it to a high degree of accuracy. A widely encompassing understanding of Fate is impossible without transcending mortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943534#post943534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey guys, there's this flaw with the system, please do your best to ignore it, okay? Suspension of disbelief and all that.&quot;<br /> &quot;But it's in the system! I'm entitled to it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey guys, there's this flaw with the system, so I've instituted these houserules so you don't have to worry whether or not you're 'exploiting' it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=943534#post943534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate likes drama. Practicing isn't dramatic enough for Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T04:42:53-07:00","id":944240,"title":"","content":"It still feels like you're overstating the &quot;in-universe&quot; knowledge being presented. Fate Sight lets you see people in the middle of extremely poor, or extremely good, moments, because those things exist in-universe. It just uses the existing dramatic failure/exceptional success mechanics to say what's significant enough to count. If your character can single out extremely injured people, and the system says to note this as people that have damage in their last 3 Health boxes, it doesn't mean they know Health boxes are a thing, or that damage is done in discrete chunks. It just a way to define in the system what's significantly injured enough to ping as, &quot;that person is seriously injured.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fate doesn't prove that exceptional successes are a real thing in-universe. It proves what we all already know: that doing really well on something is a thing in-universe. Fate just uses the out-of-universe exceptional success metric as a mechanical signpost for when doing really well is significant enough to register as notable to Fate Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T05:44:34-07:00","id":944256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=944168#post944168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey guys, there's this flaw with the system, so I've instituted these houserules so you don't have to worry whether or not you're 'exploiting' it.&quot;<br /> <br /> That works.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a solid approach.<br /> <br /> The rest of your argument seems to be hung up on conflating the purely mechanical term &quot;exceptional success&quot; with good fortune or good results that are observable, and thus can be manipulated, within the character's world.<br /> <br /> Opinions differ on the semantics of word choice and rule application. But I think going with the idea to call the Praxis Spam Nerf a house rule to be implemented as the ST deems most appropriate is the best and easiest course.<br /> <br /> This way the ST maintains some sanity at the table and having it &quot;codified&quot; in a set house rule should shut up the rules lawyers long enough to let the game proceed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:59:52-07:00","id":945079,"title":"","content":"One of our players brought up the exceptional success exploitability independently of anything on this forum recently, and his worry with it was indeed &quot;Since I'll be using my praxis often to buff other members of the group even outside of dangerous situations, I'm worried it will end up feeling exploitative.&quot; I think Strill has a good point when he wants the rule errata'd for that reason. Not everyone is comfortable figuring out their own ruling on the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:02:43-07:00","id":945116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=945079#post945079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everyone is comfortable figuring out their own ruling on the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The CofD system is pretty explicit about it being all right to come up with your own way of doing things. In addition, this is not the first time Strill has requested a very contested change in the game instead of using house rules solutions that people come up with. An example is in this thread: Axelgear gave the suggestion that you only reap the benefits of an exceptional success when in a stressful situation. It was literally the second reply to the op.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:17:11-07:00","id":945125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=945116#post945116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The CofD system is pretty explicit about it being all right to come up with your own way of doing things. In addition, this is not the first time Strill has requested a very contested change in the game instead of using house rules solutions that people come up with. An example is in this thread: Axelgear gave the suggestion that you only reap the benefits of an exceptional success when in a stressful situation. It was literally the second reply to the op.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people do not feel comfortable changing rules on their own. They buy rule products exactly so they would not have to step into that mire. I am not like that, you are presumably not like that, but there are people like that. Suggesting house rules seems like a logical step to take as we wait for this problem to be addressed, but Strill's core concern is not addressed with the house rule. His opening post is a simple request for something that is clearly broken to be added to errata. It is broken, hence, why not errata it? I do not get the hostility toward his point of view. The flaw in the rules does not bother me and is easy for me to deal with, but I'm not about to suggest that every rules problem that *I* have no problem with is not worth fixing.<br /> <br /> I feel maybe past history with this particular poster might be colouring replies in this thread, since to me, as an outside observer with no knowledge of things that might have gone before, his request seems completely reasonable, and I can't help but feel uncomfortable with the fact he's taking flak from basically everyone in the thread for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:33:55-07:00","id":945143,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I feel that book as presented is sometimes treated like a sacrosanct text, honestly. <br /> And yeah, I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T17:28:06-07:00","id":945168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=945125#post945125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel maybe past history with this particular poster might be colouring replies in this thread, since to me, as an outside observer with no knowledge of things that might have gone before, his request seems completely reasonable, and I can't help but feel uncomfortable with the fact he's taking flak from basically everyone in the thread for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe everyone in the thread is correct? <br /> <br /> Also, this is not as clear cut as appears. Essentially you are saying game designers are responsible for implementing rules that replace common sense. <br /> <br /> For example, the book doesn't say that Strill should be allowed to play this game. Perhaps the developers should address that too?<br /> <br /> The book doesn't say I shouldn't stab the ST. The book doesn't list every single spirit or ghost that exists in the world. Is that an error too? <br /> <br /> The book doesn't explain how to physically roll d10. Or what a d10 looks like.<br /> <br /> I can go on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:06:13-07:00","id":945195,"title":"","content":"Out of people I play CofD with, I'm the only one with enough know-how, understanding of game design, perception of inner-balance and gameplay foresight to attempt creating workable home rules. And perhaps, most importantly, only one willing to go down the rabbit hole and grapple with the game engine.<br /> Honestly? Each time we find something unclear, something working not-really, or something in need a home rule, it's a disappointment for us and a waste of our time. Are they all stupid/bad role players/people lacking common sense? There is nothing &quot;common sense&quot; about writing home rules or balancing games. There is nothing &quot;common sense&quot; about having inner understanding of &quot;should a 2nd dot spell be capable of producing this kind of benefit as compared to third dot spells?&quot; I really, really hate how people are overusing &quot;common sense&quot; in general; &quot;gut instincts&quot; aren't solution to everything.<br /> I mean, common sense home rules I saw were stuff like &quot;critical hits should be auto kills, because that's common sense&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-06-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:58:38-07:00","id":945218,"title":"","content":"I'll give Strill the fact that there is an issue here that probably needs to be addressed (which in turn is somewhat agreeing with the op because strill wasn't the op). The problem, though, is that Strill is fairly decent at analysis of the game while oftentimes stubborn about refusing suggestions. That's part of the point of the forums: we're here to get other people's opinions about the game as well as find solutions to our issues with it. Instead of demanding that an issue be fixed and take up time from the developers (which, by the way, is more valuable than our time), perhaps he (and others) could accept houserules that fit the lore and mechanics of the game. Taking for example this issue: the main reason that he convinced me there was a problem was that mages are the kind of people to exploit any chance for a grab at power. However, as players, my group of friends are the kind of people that enjoy a good game session over trying to work the system, so we had by default already been following the &quot;houserule&quot; of only allowing exceptional successes to benefit our characters when it mattered. <br /> <br /> Yes, it isn't necessarily consistent with the mechanics, but come on! If that is all it takes to break your immersion then you're missing the mindset of the developers (use what you need, throw away what you don't like), which is kind of important to playing the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:06:10-07:00","id":945244,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2535_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2535\" data-vbnamecard=\"2535\">arthexis</a> There's no such thing as common sense. That nitpick out of the way...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1292_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1292\" data-vbnamecard=\"1292\">Unahim</a> It's true, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> has a history here and it affects the way we interact with him. Frequently, to me at least, it feels less like I'm having a frank and useful conversation and more like an argument that runs in stubborn circles. It's true that there's this loophole in the game that could be exploited. What frustrates me most is that Strill seems to have taken the perspective that a chink in the system, because it exists, will be exploited by players to the best of their ability rather than trying to enjoy the game in a more constructive and cooperative fashion with other players and their ST. It's really pessimisitic. Sure, there are some players that will try to exploit the system, that happens. That doesn't necessarily make the mechanic itself a problem though, after all it would work just fine if there weren't that person trying to game the system. I take issue with the fact that because, hypothetically, it can be gamed means that it -will- be gamed in every group and therefore needs to be fixed when it seems obvious to me that in that situation what actually needs to happen is a change in attitude for the person trying to game the system for no other reason than that it can be gamed.<br /> <br /> In an earlier post, Strill posited a scenario in which a Mage could legitimately seek out and try to understand the &quot;Mystery&quot; of infinite Mana and WP via spamming their Praxis. Assuming I allowed that as an Obsession (Which is unlikely [And Obsessions are the mechanic I would require for actually intensively exploring a Mystery]) then I'd consider that a perfectly legitimate Mystery to try and understand. If you can make the mechanics matter to the game, then we might, in fact, be on to something. It could provide an interesting plot hook, the PC has figured out this infinite Mana and WP engine, and NPCs may notice and try to figure out how they did it for instance. To do it just for the sake of doing it though isn't something I'd allow. I don't think most STs would allow it once they realized it was happening. In my mind, it really isn't a flaw in the system that needs to be addressed as much as it is an issue that might come up because of people at the table and the problem of adjudicating how the table works falls squarely in the ST's lap. Poor bastard. That is the crux of my entire disagreement with Strill, and Earth Seraph Edna for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T21:13:53-07:00","id":945270,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Enough already. This thread topic isn't &quot;let's analyze Strill's posts and analyze Strill themself&quot;. If the back and forth arguing and off topic posts continue this thread will be closed.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T05:42:17-07:00","id":945414,"title":"","content":"Right, there is no such thing as common sense, just people more or less agreeing to what I am saying already XD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:23:09-07:00","id":949887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940787-still-no-errata-for-praxis-spam-for-recharging-mana-and-willpower?p=945244#post945244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2535_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2535\" data-vbnamecard=\"2535\">arthexis</a> There's no such thing as common sense. That nitpick out of the way...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1292_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1292\" data-vbnamecard=\"1292\">Unahim</a> It's true, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> has a history here and it affects the way we interact with him. Frequently, to me at least, it feels less like I'm having a frank and useful conversation and more like an argument that runs in stubborn circles. It's true that there's this loophole in the game that could be exploited. What frustrates me most is that Strill seems to have taken the perspective that a chink in the system, because it exists, will be exploited by players to the best of their ability rather than trying to enjoy the game in a more constructive and cooperative fashion with other players and their ST. It's really pessimisitic. Sure, there are some players that will try to exploit the system, that happens. That doesn't necessarily make the mechanic itself a problem though, after all it would work just fine if there weren't that person trying to game the system. I take issue with the fact that because, hypothetically, it can be gamed means that it -will- be gamed in every group and therefore needs to be fixed when it seems obvious to me that in that situation what actually needs to happen is a change in attitude for the person trying to game the system for no other reason than that it can be gamed.<br /> <br /> In an earlier post, Strill posited a scenario in which a Mage could legitimately seek out and try to understand the &quot;Mystery&quot; of infinite Mana and WP via spamming their Praxis. Assuming I allowed that as an Obsession (Which is unlikely [And Obsessions are the mechanic I would require for actually intensively exploring a Mystery]) then I'd consider that a perfectly legitimate Mystery to try and understand. If you can make the mechanics matter to the game, then we might, in fact, be on to something. It could provide an interesting plot hook, the PC has figured out this infinite Mana and WP engine, and NPCs may notice and try to figure out how they did it for instance. To do it just for the sake of doing it though isn't something I'd allow. I don't think most STs would allow it once they realized it was happening. In my mind, it really isn't a flaw in the system that needs to be addressed as much as it is an issue that might come up because of people at the table and the problem of adjudicating how the table works falls squarely in the ST's lap. Poor bastard. That is the crux of my entire disagreement with Strill, and Earth Seraph Edna for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason this issue sticks out to me is because the rest of the game so elegantly integrates game mechanics into the game fiction, to the point that this issue in particular stands out by the fact that it's not acknowledged.<br /> <br /> For example, you have mages generating conditions with magic to gain Beats. Do Beats exist as a tangible concept within the fiction? No. They're an abstract game conceit. Nevertheless, even though game characters cannot study Beats themselves, they can study their effects on the game world, and conclude that to become stronger, they must overcome adversity. The consequences of a Beat-based experience point system are integrated into the setting, and it even becomes a viable mystery to study. The game mechanics define the setting.<br /> <br /> There's other examples of this too. Mystery Cult Influence gives you double returns on merit dots, but that's ok because it's there to encourage mages to be the illuminati, with all that that entails. Concilium/Order status is basically a license to print merit dots, but it's there to entrap your character into the game's politics. Legacy Oblations are like getting a hallow for free on top of your legacy, but that's ok because you have to adopt strange habits that alienate you from others and make you act like a mage. Demesnes allow you to go wild with Reach, but give your character a huge weak point that can be exploited by your enemies.<br /> <br /> Every time I find something that seems &quot;overpowered&quot; or an &quot;exploit&quot;, I find a good reason for it to be that way. Either it plays into a major theme that the game is trying to emphasize, or it reveals an aspect of the game world, or it sets up dramatic plot seeds. You have all of these other &quot;overpowered&quot; game mechanics that are set up precisely in the hopes that you will exploit them, but not this one. You have those other mechanics that define parts of the setting, but with exceptional successes, you're meant to look away and ignore the setting implications. So to me, the game is purposely setting up players to take on a min-maxing mindset, and then slapping them in the face when they do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Take all the 'overpowered' merits. They'll open up tons of interesting plot hooks.&quot;<br /> &quot;Take all the negative conditions you want, but be careful they don't come back to bite you.&quot;<br /> &quot;Make a soul stone. It'll let you cast that crazy powerful spell. Don't worry about the Seers spy that's been stalking you.&quot;<br /> <br /> But then it turns around and says<br /> <br /> &quot;What, you want to cast your praxis a bunch of times to get mana? What are you, a min-maxer? Get out of here. That doesn't make any sense&quot;<br /> <br /> That to me seems wrong. You can't build a good game around encouraging the player to take all of these choices in the pursuit of power, and then say that <i>this</i> road to power is off-limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-13-2016, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:12:17-07:00","id":957532,"title":"","content":"I'd feel weird both as a player and a storyteller if the storyteller didn't use this as a juicy opportunity for drama anyhow. Imperial Mysteries talk about Siddha becoming concerned when repeated spirit magic thins the gauntlet, implying that the effects of magic aren't always neat or predictable. If a player kept doing this, I'd probably introduce all sorts of fun shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there nimbus starts flaring uncontrollably for the praxis, spreading further along their sympathetic connections then there wisdom would normally allow, as the supernal rush of clinching the imago so well every time does *whatever handwaved solution that you prefer - I'd go with bleeds their supernal gnosis over their sympathetic connections like an overfull dam*<br /> <br /> Supernal or ephemeral entities taking an interest, spontaneous opportunities for character development, such as the praxis moving back and forth between a rote and praxis based on a random roll, wierd and unusual conditions such as the spell becoming unsupressable or dispellable for a brief time, mage sight blinding effects (Like an ascended ochema, all mages see when they look at you in mage sight is the same blazing imago) and paradox anomaly esque effects all seem like an invitation to a fun time.<br /> <br /> If you want a mechanical hack, the house rule of once per scene or dramatic tension only or after the first exceptional success in the scene the storyteller chooses the benefit or the storyteller can generate new options seems appropriate. I'd probably go with crossing out each option after using it once in a scene, so players can still get every benefit, but can't experience a beautiful supernal rush thirty times a minute.<br /> <br /> If you want narrative consequences, lots of the suggestions above can give your players things to toddle off and look at under a microscope or learn to cope with the consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> I'd like to stress that it doesn't have to be a punishment if you and your players are okay with this stuff happening, but my biggest problem with the hack is that it seems really dull, so add some spice.<br /> <br /> Hopefully these suggestions can patch that part of the game for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12329-gravity-srainbro","name":"Gravity'sRainbro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:21:57-07:00","id":957536,"title":"","content":"The thing about introducing &quot;all sorts of shenanigans&quot; is that a lot of people will feel like you are punishing them and inventing rules just to kick them down, which isn't very pleasant experience. <br /> One of things I regret about Mage 2nd ED is that there isn't really much space for &quot;fair&quot; drawbacks of magic; other than paradox, there isn't a tool for game master to introduce complications and side effects of magic &quot;fairly&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:26:21-07:00","id":957540,"title":"","content":"I think introducing complications without them being perceived as punishments is could be done. Though perhaps other players then would feel as if using exploits was being rewarded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12329-gravity-srainbro","name":"Gravity'sRainbro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}